{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1485300-ceremonies-and-supernatural-merits","id":1485300,"title":"Ceremonies and supernatural merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-29T10:20:15-07:00","id":1485300,"title":"Ceremonies and supernatural merits","content":"Taking into account you can loose a supernatural merit representing a magic ritual if you are transformed into a supernatural(lile a vampire or a bound) but you mantein your ceremonies even if that happens how would you explain what is different between the two in-universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T11:26:33-07:00","id":1485304,"title":"","content":"A ceremony is like an exorcism. It's not a supernatural power internal to you. It's a ritual that, if followed correctly, harnesses the occult laws of the universe to achieve a given result. Anyone can perform a ceremony. The reason you need to buy it as a Merit is that they're not well known and have to be studied and draw on sufficient associations and symbols of power to be carried out successfully. It's the same as how anyone can physically administer medical treatments, but you need dots of Medicine to actually know how to do it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist: The Sin Eaters, p. 124</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although Sin-Eaters and their krewes make the most frequent use of Ceremonies, they aren\u2019t unique to the Bound. Ceremonies don\u2019t draw their power from the Bargain or the geist \u2014 as near as anyone can tell, they don\u2019t draw their power from anywhere: they\u2019re just a part of how the world works.<br /> The truth is, anyone can learn Ceremonies, and indeed many people know and perform at least a few regularly, even if they don\u2019t think of it as doing a \u201cmagic spell.\u201d Virtually every religion\u2019s funerary rites include the Pass On Ceremony, for example, and the Warding and Exorcism actions described in the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook are effectively Ceremonies that have become such common knowledge that they don\u2019t have a dot rating any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T14:36:26-07:00","id":1485313,"title":"","content":"Well yes, but some supernatural merits also represent rituals right?<br /> Or all of them represent internal powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T14:49:24-07:00","id":1485316,"title":"","content":"Likeforexample bless amulet from hurt locker specifies it as a ritual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T16:52:09-07:00","id":1485319,"title":"","content":"Yes, and like Bless Amulet, Supernatural Merits that are ritually based will describe themselves as rituals or otherwise have ritualistic demands for enactment.<br /> <br /> The difference is an open question, a facet of the story no one's going to answer. I implied in Memento Mori that there is a possible root difference is that all Ceremonies draw from things dragged down to the Underworld, and Mummy makes the case that a lot of commonly practiced magic falls under their conception as Open Rites, but the actual answer is &quot;Figure it out for your table.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T23:37:09-07:00","id":1485338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1485300-ceremonies-and-supernatural-merits?p=1485319#post1485319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and like Bless Amulet, Supernatural Merits that are ritually based will describe themselves as rituals or otherwise have ritualistic demands for enactment.<br /> <br /> The difference is an open question, a facet of the story no one's going to answer. I implied in Memento Mori that there is a possible root difference is that all Ceremonies draw from things dragged down to the Underworld, and Mummy makes the case that a lot of commonly practiced magic falls under their conception as Open Rites, but the actual answer is &amp;quot;Figure it out for your table.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What would your answer be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T10:48:59-07:00","id":1485395,"title":"","content":"As a ST, my ruling has been that the character keeps any externally derived merits: relics, rituals, it\u2019s all good, and I often err on the side of letting them keep it. If a power reads as internally derived, that\u2019s lost (or sometimes changed) in the transformation. That\u2019s very much a case by case basis, but one rule of thumb is if the power has a willpower cost - that usually indicates it\u2019s some kind of inner psychic effort.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re having a hard time judging if it should be retained try asking questions like these:<br /> - Is there some patron entity providing this when invoked? Will the character retain their favor after the transformation?<br /> - Does it cost willpower, relate to integrity, or seem to come from their intrinsic humanity? Assume this has been irrevocably warped<br /> - Can their new template replicate a power like this? Perhaps give them a discount toward buying that power as a replacement (as per sanctity of merits)<br /> - Does the merit rely on some kind of occult understanding of the universe (whether the character knows it or not)? How does their transformation change their understanding of those rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T11:07:01-07:00","id":1485396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anyoneatall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1485300-ceremonies-and-supernatural-merits?p=1485338#post1485338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would your answer be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dependent on my game that I was running.<br /> <br /> So here's the thing about Ceremonies-despite my personal train of thought for Memento Mori, the big thing about them is that their main feature, outside of their utility as glue for the Krewe and their hammer and nails for a universe all up on ends, is that they are <i>not</i> from the Underworld. Because you cannot destroy the house with the Master's Tools, one of the things about Geist is that all the conventional tools you have for metaphysically challenging the Underworld sort of need to be suspect for doing-you yourself have a suspect element, to anyone with an idiot view on the subject, because you yourself are dead and therefore are the subject of the Underworld. Being Bound is a fraught condition (for a lot of reasons, not just this), and uncertainity and doubt feeding despair is very much part of the game.<br /> <br /> However, Geist is still a game about hope in the face of death and a cruel, uncaring universe, and it needs something to stop it from eating itself into being a knock-off Wraith or Mummy: the Curse*, but at the same time that something is not free from the fact that Chronicles is a horror game and nothing comes with certainty. The answer the developers landed on was the current setup of Ceremonies, where in the one thing Sin-Eaters know is that it's not from the Underworld, and that's usually enough for them-that gives them hope and agency and action.<br /> <br /> And here's the thing-it kind of doesn't actually matter why Ceremonies work, and if they do so differently to ritualistic Supernatural Merits, and if act the same then what the hell drives it all-at least, it doesn't for the terms of defining the default status quo of the world of Chronicles. There is <i>some</i> difference, obviously, but the need to explore that line just doesn't come up unless there's a game deriving meaning out of it.<br /> <br /> On the mechanical side of things, THe Supernatural Merit lockdown is there to keep gamelines fom doing things too terribly wonky and out of line for their themes and ideas, while Ceremonies were designed to allow Krewe to operate without strictly needing Sin-Eaters, and ended up with a nice benefit of allowing crosover where monsters who research this or join Krewes can be necromancer/urgists in their own right.<br /> <br /> Anyways, tl;dr of this is &quot;it depends on why it matters to your story and table.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Alternate Endgames outside of Apotheosis were bad choices, if I've never said that out loud before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T12:09:01-07:00","id":1485402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1485300-ceremonies-and-supernatural-merits?p=1485396#post1485396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Alternate Endgames outside of Apotheosis were bad choices, if I've never said that out loud before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for the off-topic aside here: strongly cosigned. I understand Mummy 2e's desire to be more flexible, but for all the flaws I found in it (and I found many), Mummy 1e was committed to suggesting a strong core arc from blindly wielded might to understanding and self-definition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}